{title: 595 - Let Every Lamp Be Burning}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Let every lamp be burning bright,
[Ab]The [Eb]darkest [Bb7]hour is [Eb]near[Bb]ing;
[Bb7]The [Eb]darkest hour of earth’s long night,
[Ab]Be[Eb]fore the [Bb7]Lord’s appear[Eb]ing.
[Eb]Then trim your lamps, my [Ab]brethren [Eb]dear,
Then trim your lamps with godly [Bb]fear;
[Bb7]The [Cm]Master’s coming [Eb]draweth near,
[Ab]Let [Eb]every [Bb7]lamp be burn[Eb]ing.

Refrain:
[Eb]Then trim your lamps, my brethren dear,
[Ab]Then [Eb]trim [Bb7]your lamps [Eb]with [Bb]godly fear;
[Bb7]The Master's [Eb]coming draweth near,
[Ab]Let [Eb]every [Bb7]lamp [Eb]be burning.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Though thousands calmly slumber on,
[Ab]The [Eb]last [Bb7]great [Eb]message [Bb]spuring,
[Bb7]Wel'll rest our [Eb]living faith upon
[Ab]His [Eb]promise [Bb7]of [Eb]returning.

Verse 3:
[Eb]His word our lamp, His truth our guide,
[Ab][Eb]We [Bb7]cannot [Eb]be [Bb]mistaken;
[Bb7]Though dangers rise [Eb]on every side,
[Ab]We [Eb]shall [Bb7]not [Eb]be forsaken.

Verse 4:
[Eb]Then let good works with faith appear,
[Ab]To [Eb]help [Bb7]the [Eb]world [Bb]atound us;
[Bb7]Obedience bring [Eb]the blessing near
[Ab]When [Eb]faith has [Bb7]firmly [Eb]bound us.
